Nivel de vechime: Nivel mediu de experiență
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Dezvoltare de software
As a Level 2 Senior IP Support Engineer you will be managing the core IP network nodes and services. You will be responsible for troubleshooting issues, configuration changes, as well as controlling access to the network.
 This role is part of a team of 3 L2 IP engineers and a bigger team of 14 engineers reporting to the same Team Lead, NOC, Engineering.
 This role is based in Bucharest, with a hybrid work model requiring at least 2 days per week in the office (The Bridge 3, Sector 6).
 Key Responsibilities 
 Implementation & Configuration : Coordinate, support, and execute new implementations or changes to the existing standard services on IP areas and relevant internal tools;
Change Management: Follow the established Change Management process and ensure that all changes are tracked and properly documented. You will be responsible for creating and owning the change requests for any modifications you implement;
 Troubleshooting & Issue Resolution : You will schedule and participate in troubleshooting sessions with partners and customers when necessary.;
 Knowledge Transfer : Participate in knowledge transfer sessions with other teams to stay updated on new solutions, product changes, or updates that affect this team’s implementation. Provide knowledge transfer when necessary to other teams;
 Documentation & Procedure Management: Maintain and regularly update the collection of implementation procedures to ensure they align with current best practices and technology updates. Act as the single point of contact for our partners regarding standard service requests related to IP domain implementations. Provide clear communication and timely resolutions;
 Ticket Management : Receive, acknowledge, and work on tickets raised by our customers and partners within the IP domain. You will be responsible for ensuring that tickets are handled efficiently and within the agreed-upon SLAs;
 Escalation Management : Create, monitor, and follow-up on escalation tickets, directing them to the second-level or partner management teams when necessary. Ensure that issues are resolved within appropriate timelines and that stakeholders are kept informed. 
 Qualifications 
 Educational Background: 
Completed education (University degree) in Telecommunications, Computer Science, or a related field is preferred;
Experience: Minimum of 3-5 years of experience in a network support or engineering role, particularly in IP networks.
 Technical Skills: 
Experience with network equipment and technologies such as Juniper, Ericsson, Extreme Networks (routers, switches, firewalls);
Strong knowledge of VPN technologies (IPsec, MPLS VPN) and network configuration;
Hands-on experience with network monitoring tools like Grafana, Cacti, or similar platforms;
Familiarity with DNS (BIND) and GGSN/PGW (Ericsson) services;
Experience using tracing tools for troubleshooting network issues.
 Key Competencies: 
Analytical technical thinking and problem-solving skills;
Strong communication and collaboration abilities;
Perseverance and a proactive approach to troubleshooting and documenting technical solutions;
Ability to react quickly in a fast-paced environment and provide clear, effective support;
A passion for advising, assisting, and developing others, with a professional and tactful approach;
Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively.
 Language Proficiency: Proficiency in English (both written and spoken).
 Our Process 
30 min Talent Team Discussion – Teams;
60 min Interview with the Hiring Manager & N+1 – On-Site.
 Please note that this reflects the current agreed interview process and may be adjusted or updated as the recruitment process progresses. 
 Additional Benefits 
25 + days Vacation;
Health Insurance Private plan (EE+ Dependents);
Life Insurance;
Lunch Allowance;
Home Internet WFH supplement. 
 Why Aeris? 
Work on large-scale, mission-critical IoT and connectivity networks supporting millions of devices worldwide.
Join a highly technical and collaborative operations team with strong exposure to IP networking, troubleshooting, and global operations.
Be part of a company at the forefront of Physical AI, connected mobility, and next-generation IoT innovation.
 Aeris is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, marital status, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected status.
